Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||09-19-1999||12:24 PM||||heres some symptoms, lessee if anyone can gimme an idea about whats wrong<P>1)('86 SE 2M6) my car overheats quickly<BR>2)i get about 11mpg around town, 18 on the freeway<BR>3)fiero doesn't seem to pull as hard as my friend's fiero<BR>4)idles between 1500 and 2100 rpm, makes a constant popping sound at the muffler (not backfiring... there IS a crack in the muffler, tho)<P>the things i have done are: replaced the thermostat, burped the cooling system, replaced all the gaskets down to the rocker arm ones... and my car is a bitch to get running unless i let it warm up for like 15 minutes||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||09-19-1999||01:59 PM||||If you have allot of TIME on your hands you might want to put some of it into your motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-19-1999||02:48 PM||||Cold operation problems, overheat, and high idle point towards a lean mixture or incorrect timing.  If there are no codes indicating a bad oxygen sensor or IAC valve, then a vacuum leak is a likely culprit(ie..cracked EGR tube).<P>The other symtoms you describe are probably due to a different issue, hopefully just a clogged cat. converter. If this is not the case, it may be time for a compression check.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-19-1999||07:52 PM||||I vote for an intake leak and a possible dead O2. The popping could very well be unburnt fuel burning in the exhaust.<P>Is the CE/SES lamp on?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||09-20-1999||12:30 PM||||Have you checked for a clogged catalytic converter?||||reg||1
